{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_ZqdLoCcjcU846Tx6BPERbiwK","content":"Title: add_or_update_event - Intervals.icu MCP Server\nSite: glama.ai\nDate: 2026-09-06\nURL: https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/csikosaron98/intervals-mcp-server/tools/add_or_update_event\nSnippet: Create or update a training event on Intervals.icu by providing workout ... icu this follows the event api from intervals. ... units\": \"%ftp\"}, \"duration\": 900, \" ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals.icu Workout Format — ZonePace\nURL: https://zonepace.cc/intervals-workout-format\nSnippet: Cadence (Cycling) ``` - 10m 75% 90rpm - 5m 88% 70rpm - 12m 85% 90-100rpm ``` Repeats Two forms are supported: - In a section header: `Main Set 5x` - Standalone line before a block: `5x` Notes: Nested repeats aren’t officially supported. Only header lines or standalone `nx` define repeats; occurrences inside descriptive text are ignored. Text Prompts - Any text before the first duration/intensity becomes the step cue. - Repeated blocks append `k/N` to the first step’s text (e.g., _Main set 1/6_).\n\n---\n\nTitle: Workout steps inside repeat blocks show as \"Other\" in Garmin - Bug Reports - Intervals.icu Forum\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2026-03-12\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-steps-inside-repeat-blocks-show-as-other-in-garmin/124473\nSnippet: post by Kavana on 12 Mar When creating structured workouts with repeat blocks (e.g., 6x 800m), the steps inside the repeat block show as “Other” type in Garmin devices, instead of showing the correct step type (Interval, Recovery, etc.). Steps to Reproduce Create a workout in Intervals.icu with a repeat block, for example: 复制 Warmup - 1km Run @ 6:30/km Main Set 6x - 0.8km Run @ 4:45/km - 0.4km Run @ 7:00/km Cooldown - 1km Run @ 6:30/km Sync the workout to Garmin Connect 1. View the workout on Ga\n\n---\n\nTitle: API access to Intervals.icu - Page 22 - Guide\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2020-04-01\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=22\nSnippet: ... workout_doc\": { \"steps\": [ { \"reps\": 1, \"text\": \"1X\", \"steps\": [ { \"duration\": 600, \"power\": { \"end\": 80, \"start\": 65, \"units\": \"%ftp ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: FIT workout import silently drops REPS steps and mis-scales DISTANCE steps - Bug Reports - Intervals.icu Forum\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2026-08-21\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/fit-workout-import-silently-drops-reps-steps-and-mis-scales-distance-steps/131081\nSnippet: t at all. hr_zone target exports as a wrong absolute range: a workout_doc step with hr: {value: 2, units: \"hr_zone\"} (real HR zone 2) exported ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: API access to Intervals.icu - Page 4 - Guide\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2020-04-01\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=4\nSnippet: \"workout_doc\": { \"steps\": [ { \"power\": {\"units\": \"%ftp\", \"value\": 60}, \"cadence\": {\"end\": 100, \"start\": 90, \"units\": \"rpm\"}, \"duration ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: API access to Intervals.icu - Guide\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2020-04-01\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609\nSnippet: \"workout_doc\": { \"steps\": [ { \"power\": {\"units\": \"%ftp\", \"value\": 60}, \"cadence\": {\"end\": 100, \"start\": 90, \"units\": \"rpm\"}, \"duration ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: API access to Intervals.icu - Page 7 - Guide\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2020-04-01\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7\nSnippet: ... steps\": [ { \"duration\": 600, \"power\": { \"value\": 43, \"units\": \"%ftp\" } }, { \"duration\": 900, \"power\": { \"value\": 65, \"units\": \"%ftp ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Training Plans in Intervals.icu — Create, Share & Export\nSite: STAS\nDate: 2026-04-05\nURL: https://stas.run/en/guides/intervals-icu-training-plans\nSnippet: Every workout is a structured sequence of steps — warm-up, intervals, cool-down ... Wahoo ELEMNT head units connect via Settings → Connections → Wahoo.\n\n---\n\nTitle: How to send structured workouts with repeats and pace/power ranges via API? - Uncategorized - Intervals.icu Forum\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2026-08-11\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/how-to-send-structured-workouts-with-repeats-and-pace-power-ranges-via-api/130971\nSnippet: Thanks! mreno 11 August 2026 22:38 2. I tried this: curl -X POST . “https://intervals.icu/api ... units”:“secs/km”},“duration”:600},{“reps”:2,“ ...\n\nWhen you rely on a result in your answer, cite it inline as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url)."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_zk1g48YPtyfpCmupMthvPC3J","content":"Title: GitHub - Sladck/trainingpeaks-to-intervals-icu: Sync planned TrainingPeaks workouts to intervals.icu with structured power/pace/HR targets\nSite: Github\nDate: 2026-05-20\nURL: https://github.com/Sladck/trainingpeaks-to-intervals-icu\nSnippet: What it syncs Permalink: What it syncs |TrainingPeaks side|becomes on intervals.icu| |-|-| |Planned workout (Bike / Run / Swim / MTB / Strength / …)|`WORKOUT` event with sport-correct type| |Structured intervals ( `%FTP`, `%LTHR`, `%threshold pace`)|`workout_doc` with absolute watts / bpm / s/km, computed from your TP thresholds| |Workout `description` (coach text)|event description (+ pushed into paired `activity.description`)| |`coachComments`|\"Coach:\" section in description| |`workoutComments\n\n---\n\nTitle: GitHub - platypus45/domestique: Adaptive cycling training planner: 7 science-grounded injury-prevention guardrails close the loop between planned and actual training. 4,232 ZWO workouts, 622 routes, h\nSite: Github\nDate: 2026-10-23\nURL: https://github.com/platypus45/domestique\nSnippet: What's new in v3 Push to intervals.icu. Send your planned workouts straight to your intervals.icu calendar (one-off button on the Training Plan tab, or an optional keep-in-sync setting) so Garmin & MyWhoosh pull them automatically — and any single workout too: every workout detail view (planner or library) has a send-to-calendar button, with a date picker for library workouts; heart-rate plans push with HR targets. Only Domestique's own entries are ever touched — your races and anything you adde\n\n---\n\nTitle: intervals-mcp by ale7canna\nSite: glama.ai\nDate: 2026-08-20\nURL: https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/ale7canna/intervals-mcp\nSnippet: Come arrivano gli allenamenti sul Garmin 1. `create_workout` scrive un evento `category: \"WORKOUT\"` sul calendario; il campo `description` contiene l'allenamento nella sintassi testuale di intervals.icu. 2. intervals.icu lo interpreta e ne costruisce la struttura ( `workout_doc`). 3. Se su intervals.icu → Settings, nel box Garmin, è attivo Upload planned workouts (con Garmin Connect autorizzato), i prossimi giorni di calendario vengono caricati su Garmin Connect e da lì arrivano all'orologio. 4.\n\n---\n\nTitle: garmin-mcp-bridge | MCP Servers\nSite: lobehub.com\nDate: 2026-07-19\nURL: https://lobehub.com/it/mcp/jonas-theobald-garmin-mcp-bridge\nSnippet: Writing workouts Permalink for this section The workout_doc trap Permalink for this section Never include a `workout_doc` field in the payload. A planned workout only syncs to your watch if Intervals.icu parsed the description into structured steps. What triggers that parsing is undocumented, and the intuitive guess is wrong: sending `workout_doc: {}` to _request_ parsing actually suppresses it. The server reads the presence of the field as \"steps already supplied\" and skips the parser. The work\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals Workout · GarminFans\nSite: GarminFans\nDate: 2026-11-07\nURL: https://www.garminfans.com/fi/apps/8f9714b5-9367-4424-b086-30711f0d9632/\nSnippet: Kuvaus Intervals Workout is a Data Field for Edge 540 and 1050 that reads your Intervals.icu structured workout and guides you in real time, step by step. At a glance: • Current target watts (blue) + 3s actual power (green/red at ±15 W) • Heart rate color-coded by zone (gray, blue, green, orange, red by % of threshold) • Cadence with target (e.g. \"target 90 rpm\") — green ±5, orange ±10, red beyond • Step name + position (e.g. \"Ramp 50 to 75 %FTP 1/10\") • Step time remaining + total time • Per-st\n\n---\n\nTitle: Structured running workouts from intervals to Garmin Connect - Uncategorized - Intervals.icu Forum\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2026-07-17\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/structured-running-workouts-from-intervals-to-garmin-connect/130705\nSnippet: intervals drops the per-step pace targets on the Garmin export (falls back to HR), hence “No Target”. use the API to upload workouts as well\n\n---\n\nTitle: Exact HR corridors on Garmin from Intervals.icu API workouts\nSite: Worklore\nDate: 2026-05-12\nURL: https://worklore.dev/s/2026-05-12-exact-hr-corridors-on-garmin-from-intervals-icu-api-workouts\nSnippet: My AI agent generates structured triathlon workouts and pushes them to Intervals.icu via POST /events ; Intervals FIT-exports them to my Garmin ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Athlete help — PaceTrack\nSite: PaceTrack\nDate: 2026-11-01\nURL: https://pacetrack.cc/en/help-athlete.php\nSnippet: 8. Profile Copy link to this section “Profile” Tab - Training Zones — a link to `/athlete/training-zones.php` where you set running HR zones (Z1–Z5, Recovery → Maximum) and pace zones (Z1–Z5, mm:ss/km). Used by your coach when building structured workouts with zone-based steps. You can set values manually, calculate them from anchor values (max HR, LTHR, threshold pace), or import directly from Garmin Connect (only when it is connected the previous way, see 7.1) or Intervals.icu (if connected, s\n\n---\n\nTitle: Domestique - a free, open source, science based, self hosted cycling training app - Training - TrainerRoad\nSite: TrainerRoad\nDate: 2026-06-14\nURL: https://www.trainerroad.com/forum/t/domestique-a-free-open-source-science-based-self-hosted-cycling-training-app/113958\nSnippet: post by Domestique1 on Jul 6 100% Free, open source, locally hosted training cycling planner. Science based. What’s new since the last post, grouped: Train by heart rate — no power meter needed. The biggest addition. A workout-targets mode that prescribes every session in bpm: LTHR-anchored ranges for steady work, RPE for short maximal efforts (HR lags too much there, and the app tells you so instead of pretending). LTHR syncs continuously from intervals.icu with a manual override, zones are cus\n\n---\n\nTitle: Coach help — PaceTrack\nSite: PaceTrack\nDate: 2026-06-15\nURL: https://pacetrack.cc/help.php\nSnippet: 9. Athlete Profile 9.12. Athlete Training Zones The \"Training zones\" link in a registered athlete's profile opens `/athlete/training-zones.php` on their behalf — here you can view and edit their running HR and pace zones. - Z1–Z5 HR zones: min/max heart rate for each zone (Recovery → Maximum). - Z1–Z5 pace zones: \"slower\" and \"faster\" (mm:ss/km) for each zone. - \"Calculate & import\" panel: enter anchor values (max HR, LTHR, threshold pace) and auto-calculate zone boundaries from presets; the \"Lo\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals.icu and Garmin sync for right intensities - Training\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2024-02-05\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-and-garmin-sync-for-right-intensities/59698\nSnippet: I want to make sure that if I am setting zones for my athlete in intervals.icu they should reflect the same on Garmin either via direct sync or ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect - Page 8\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2020-08-18\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521?page=8\nSnippet: You can link your Garmin Connect account and Intervals.icu will upload your next week of planned workouts. HR zones also the same. ing beats ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: API access to Intervals.icu - Page 22 - Guide\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2020-04-01\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=22\nSnippet: Intervals.icu now has a public API for other applications. actual watts, bpm and m/s values for power, hr and pace steps. bpm or m/s are ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: intervals.icu setup guide — Coach AMA\nURL: https://coach-ama.com/guide/intervals\nSnippet: Get your training data flowing to Coach AMA In the same Connections box, enable Upload planned workouts when your service supports it. This is the return path that sends Coach AMA's [AMA] sessions from the intervals.icu calendar to your training app or head unit. 1. ## 4. If you ride in Zwift Connect the Zwift box and enable both Download activities and Upload planned workouts. In Zwift, find synced sessions under Workouts → Custom → Intervals.icu; today's session may also appear on the home scr\n\nWhen you rely on a result in your answer, cite it inline as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url)."}
