{"role":"assistant","content":"Output looks right. Now writing ANSWER.md:","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_5rYE2BAmuOJuwRZdqOOdgRHN","function":{"name":"Write","arguments":"{\"path\":\"ANSWER.md\",\"content\":\"# Fix: HR corridors clamped to the watch's zones\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\n`gen.py` emitted HR targets as `{\\\"units\\\": \\\"%lthr\\\", \\\"value\\\": <lo>, \\\"end\\\": <hi>}`.\\nThe `value`/`end` key shape is the problem: at FIT-export time Intervals.icu\\nroutes it as a Lap-HR / zone-mapped target, so the Garmin watch clamps each\\ncorridor to its own zone bands (computed from the watch's auto-detected\\nLTHR 168) instead of the planned range. That is exactly what\\n`readback/watch-notes.md` shows — every step displayed as a watch zone edge,\\nnever 151–160 or 129–141, and changing the watch's LTHR only moved the bands.\\n\\nThe two earlier attempts failed for related reasons: `units: \\\"bpm\\\"` with\\nabsolute values is misread by the FIT export as percent-of-something (hence the\\nimpossible 214–249 bpm), and `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` are not schema fields at\\nall (silently dropped, leaving Garmin's constant-101 \\\"no valid HR target\\\"\\nfallback).\\n\\n## The change\\n\\n`gen.py`, function `hr_target` — one-word change: the lower bound is now\\n`start` instead of `value`:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"units\\\": \\\"%lthr\\\", \\\"start\\\": <lo>, \\\"end\\\": <hi>}\\n```\\n\\nWith `start`/`end` the target routes as an **Instant-HR corridor**: Intervals\\nconverts the percentages using the LTHR stored in Intervals (172) at export\\ntime, and the watch displays that raw bpm range — immune to the watch's own\\nauto-detected LTHR. This is also the key shape used in Intervals' own API\\nexamples for ranged targets.\\n\\nNothing else changed: plans stay in %LTHR, units stay `%lthr` (absolute bpm\\nstays broken — don't reintroduce it), durations/repeats/labels are untouched.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json` produces valid JSON with every `hr`\\n  target as `start`/`end` (68–75, 88–93, 75–82, 65–72).\\n- Expected on-watch rendering after re-pushing and Garmin sync (Intervals\\n  LTHR 172): warm-up 117–129, tempo 151–160, float 129–141, cool-down\\n  112–124 bpm.\\n\\nRoot cause and fix corroborated by\\n[Exact HR corridors on Garmin from Intervals.icu API workouts](https://worklore.dev/s/2026-05-12-exact-hr-corridors-on-garmin-from-intervals-icu-api-workouts)\\n(same symptom, same failed attempts, verified fix) and Intervals.icu's API\\ndocumentation.\\n\\n## Follow-up not done\\n\\nThat source also flags that the Intervals **web UI** renders steps from a\\nseparate top-level `description` in Intervals' text grammar (not from\\n`workout_doc`), so without one the steps may be invisible in the UI even\\nthough the API accepts the event and the watch shows the workout. That is a\\ndisplay concern only, separate from the watch-clamping bug fixed here, so I\\nleft it alone — worth handling later with care, since a malformed description\\ncan make Intervals wipe the parsed workout.\\n\"}"}}]}
