{"role":"assistant","content":"Done. Only `gen.py` was modified and `ANSWER.md` added — nothing was pushed or reported anywhere.\n\n**Root cause:** the generator sent HR targets as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. The `value`/`end` shape routes the FIT export as a zone-mapped target, so the watch clamps every corridor to its own zone bands (built from its auto-detected LTHR 168). That's why you always saw 118–137, 151–162, etc., and why fixing the watch LTHR only moved the bands. Your two earlier attempts failed for adjacent reasons: `units: \"bpm\"` with absolute values is mis-scaled by the FIT export (the impossible 214–249), and `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` aren't real schema fields (silently dropped → Garmin's constant-101 fallback).\n\n**Fix** (`gen.py:13`): one-word change — the lower bound is now `start` instead of `value`, i.e. `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. With `start`/`end` the target exports as an Instant-HR corridor: Intervals converts the percentages using its own stored LTHR (172) and the watch displays the raw bpm range, ignoring its local zones. This matches Intervals' own API examples for ranged targets and is corroborated by [this writeup of the identical bug](https://worklore.dev/s/2026-05-12-exact-hr-corridors-on-garmin-from-intervals-icu-api-workouts).\n\n**Verified:** `python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json` emits valid JSON with all four `hr` targets as `start`/`end`. After a re-push and Garmin sync, the watch should show 117–129 / 151–160 / 129–141 / 112–124 bpm instead of the zone bands. One thing I could not verify end-to-end: actually pushing and watching the display, since the ground rules forbid external calls — so the on-watch rendering remains to be confirmed by you on the next sync.\n\nANSWER.md also notes a follow-up I deliberately didn't implement: the Intervals web UI renders steps from a separate top-level `description` in Intervals' text grammar, so the steps may be invisible in the UI even though the API accepts them — display-only, unrelated to the watch bug."}
